# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# developer added
.build
.DS_Store
.vscode
fyne-cross/

# `go build ./cmd/...` without -o can drop an extension-less binary at repo
# root named after a dev-tool command; keep those out.
/rcprobe
/rcreconcile
/sampleingest

# Live RegattaCentral API captures from cmd/rcprobe contain athlete PII and a
# real access token. Never commit them; committed test fixtures are hand-authored
# and redacted. See cmd/rcprobe/README.md.
/internal/regattacentral/testdata/
rc-secrets*.json

# cmd/rcreconcile's reports and upload previews name real athletes/schools
# from a real regatta. A catch-all local output directory - point --report-out
# / --upload-preview-out here. See cmd/rcreconcile/README.md.
/out/

# Real race-day workbooks feed cmd/sampleingest once, on a developer machine,
# and name real schools and athletes. Only the obfuscated fixture it writes
# (internal/sample/data/) is committed - keep source workbooks in
# /sample-source/ or name them *.source.xlsm. A root-level .xlsm is ignored
# too; the public example workbooks live under examples/.
# See docs/features/testing/sample-regatta.md.
/sample-source/
*.source.xlsm
/*.xlsm
